  message: "Completed WI-lozug across four PRs (2026-04-22 session):\n\n- PR 1 (Go, commit 1549c8850): emit_module_attribute_refs wired into\n  _extract_edges_from_file in go.py. node_kinds=selector_expression,\n  operand/field. Real-repo check on alertmanager (12MB, 261 .go files):\n  568 module_attr_ref edges emitted; io-boundaries reports 10 ipc_send\n  chains (5× os.Stdout, 5× os.Stderr), 2 ipc_recv (os.Stdin), 1\n  env_read (runtime.GOOS) — all previously zero.\n\n- PR 2 (JS/TS, commit 2de7f77fc): helper wired into Pass-2 loop of\n  _analyze_javascript_impl in js_ts.py. node_kinds=member_expression,\n  object/property. Merges namespace_imports + named_imports; injects\n  Node/browser globals process/window/document/navigator. Uses the\n  Pass-1 <module:filename> symbol as caller. Real-repo check on\n  ghostfolio (38MB TypeScript): 758 module_attr_ref edges; env_read\n  boundary reports 30 chains spanning process.env (13), window.location\n  (11), document.location (4), document.cookie (1), navigator.language\n  (1).\n\n- PR 3 (Java, commit d69a95399): helper wired into Pass-2 loop of\n  _analyze_java_impl in java.py. node_kinds=field_access, object/field.\n  'System' injected as implicit java.lang import. Deliberate design\n  deviation: callee-skip is DISABLED for Java because System.out is\n  typically the object of method_invocation (System.out.println), and\n  io_boundary tags callee name (println) against the catalog, not\n  receiver name — if we skipped System.out when it's a receiver, the\n  attributes: [out] entry would never match. Real-repo check on\n  spring-petclinic (2.5MB): 21 module_attr_ref edges on imported\n  enums/constants (FetchType.EAGER, Locale.ENGLISH, HttpStatus.OK).\n  No ipc_send chains because petclinic uses SLF4J loggers (0 System.out\n  usages).\n\n- PR 4 (Rust deferral, commit 89217c923): Rust's tree-sitter path is\n  intentionally left un-wired because std::env::consts::OS is\n  scoped_identifier, not field_expression — the helper's default walk\n  can't match it. Installed a regression-guard test asserting zero\n  emission today (flips to positive when the follow-up lands). The\n  rust-analyzer optional backend is unaffected.\n\nFollow-ups filed during this ticket:\n- WI-vipur-noguv-tonon-jofuh-kifir-jinuh-kotih-dujaf — cross-language\n  scoped-path mode for the helper (covers Rust tree-sitter + C++\n  qualified_identifier + Groovy + Kotlin scoped_identifier).\n- WI-gotuv-zuvob-kunij-girak-mudaz-fahol-tisir-zofud — C bare-identifier\n  stdio matching (stdout/stderr/stdin globals; helper can't match\n  because they are not member-expressions in C).\n\nPlan file: /home/jgstern_agent/.claude/plans/zany-tumbling-plum.md.\nLab journals at ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04222026_{1808,1830,1915}.md.\n\nCHANGELOG.md [Unreleased] has four WI-lozug PR entries under\nAnalysis quality; docs/hypergumbo-spec.md §Taint-flow-analysis updated\nto enumerate covered languages and note the two pending tree-sitter\ncases (Rust / C) with links to the follow-up items."  # 7d2d
